<node id="11127314" title="Re^3: I am confused by a &quot;Learning Perl&quot; sample showing &quot;unshift&quot;" created="2021-01-22 17:41:07" updated="2021-01-22 17:41:07" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="708738">LanX</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">For reasons of symmetry this&lt;P&gt;

&lt;c&gt;unshift @a, @b&lt;/c&gt; means &lt;C&gt;@a = ( @b, @a )&lt;/C&gt;&lt;P&gt;

Much the same way as&lt;P&gt;

&lt;c&gt;push @a, @b&lt;/c&gt; means &lt;C&gt;@a = ( @a, @b )&lt;/C&gt;&lt;P&gt;

So no implicit reversing of @b.&lt;P&gt;

HTH :)&lt;P&gt;




